issues.problematic_code_snippet:
abstract class TauriActivity : WryActivity() {
  var pluginManager: PluginManager = PluginManager(this)
  override val handleBackNavigation: Boolean = true

findings.body:
In the `setup` closure, `let handle_ref = &handle;` followed by `AppPlugin(*handle_ref)` tries to move a value out of a shared borrow. `PluginHandle<R>` only derives `Debug` (`crates/tauri/src/plugin.rs:124`), so it is not `Copy` and this will not compile for `target_os = "android"`. The `handle` is already owned, so the reference is unnecessary. The fix is to move it directly.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/app/plugin.rs" lines="134-143"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Desktop and host builds skip this block under `#[cfg]`, so this error will not appear in normal CI. It only shows up when the Android target is compiled.

Suggested replacement:

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri/src/app/plugin.rs" lines="137-139"}
let handle = _api.register_android_plugin("app.tauri", "AppPlugin")?;
_app.manage(AppPlugin(handle));

`AppPlugin.exit` is annotated `@Command`, but this PR does not add a permission entry for it to `core:app`, and no TypeScript or Rust wrapper calls it. Tauri's ACL denies commands that have no permission, so the method is dead code. The changelog ('Added mobile app plugin to support exit and back button press event') suggests exit is a supported feature, which is not true yet.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/mobile/android/src/main/java/app/tauri/AppPlugin.kt" lines="47-54"}

Either wire `exit` through the ACL and add a JS API, or remove it and correct the changelog.
